# Squash-merge pull requests

Land every PR as **one squashed commit** on the base branch. Do not use merge commits or plain rebase that keeps each WIP commit.

## How
- Merge via squash: `gh pr merge <pr> --squash` (or the "Squash and merge" button). To let it merge once checks pass, add `--auto`.
- Write a clean squashed commit: a clear title (imperative, matches the PR) and a short body; drop noise like `fixup`, `wip`, and `address review`.
- Keep the branch itself as normal incremental commits while iterating; squashing happens only at merge time.

## Why
- One commit per PR keeps `main` history linear, readable, and easy to revert or bisect.
